# Brand, Languages, and UI

## Business

Nora Group is a premium custom carpentry and interior-design business.

Public services may include: kitchens; wardrobes and wall-to-wall closets; dressing rooms; custom furniture; interior wood design; exterior wood design.

- Do **not** add doors as a Nora Group service.
- Do **not** reintroduce door-related marketing copy unless explicitly requested.
- Preserve the premium, architectural, modern, minimal, and sophisticated brand direction.

## Languages

- Website languages: Hebrew, Arabic, English, and Russian.
- Dashboard UI: Arabic, Hebrew, and English (Russian only if the implementation stays clean).
- Handle RTL/LTR correctly. Arabic/Hebrew content must not break layout, forms, navigation, or typography.
- Do not mix translated strings into unrelated business logic.
- Do not destroy existing translations when adding or modifying languages.

## UI / UX

- Preserve the luxury / minimal / architectural visual identity. Avoid generic templates and visual clutter.
- Dark and Light modes must both be professional and accessible. Avoid theme flashing on initial page load.
- Maintain responsive behavior across mobile, tablet, and desktop.
- Do not introduce breaking layout changes without checking all supported languages and RTL/LTR layouts.
